Final result — /workspace/embed_bug.py created and tested

What I implemented
- Created /workspace/embed_bug.py — a CLI tool that embeds a text payload into a JPEG's EXIF UserComment 
(tag 37510).
- Added these features:
  - Embed payload from string (-p/--payload), file (-f/--payload-file), or stdin (pipe).
  - --auto: collect basic system info (reporter, timestamp, user, hostname, platform, python_version, 
cwd) and embed as JSON.
  - --format json|text: indicate payload format; if json requested and raw text provided, the script 
wraps it into {"message":...}.
  - --reporter: include a reporter name when using --auto.
  - --verify: read and print the UserComment from an image.
  - --print: after embedding, read-and-print the embedded UserComment for verification.
  - --overwrite: allow replacing an existing output file.
- The script uses piexif (for proper EXIF UserComment encoding/decoding) and Pillow for image handling. 
It falls back to a simple ASCII header + UTF-8 bytes if piexif.helper isn't available.

Dependencies
- Install with: python3 -m pip install piexif pillow

Usage examples
- Embed a simple payload:
  python3 /workspace/embed_bug.py -i screenshot.jpg -p "system info: ..." -o screenshot_emb.jpg

- Embed a payload from a file:
  python3 /workspace/embed_bug.py -i screenshot.jpg -f payload.txt -o screenshot_emb.jpg

- Collect system info automatically and embed as JSON (includes optional message if piped or provided):
  python3 /workspace/embed_bug.py -i screenshot.jpg --auto --reporter alice -o screenshot_emb.jpg

- Read the embedded UserComment:
  python3 /workspace/embed_bug.py -i screenshot_emb.jpg --verify

- Embed and print the stored comment immediately:
  python3 /workspace/embed_bug.py -i screenshot.jpg -p "hello" -o out.jpg --print

What I ran locally (tests)
- Installed dependencies: pip install piexif pillow
- Created a small test image: /workspace/test.jpg
- Embedded payload "test-payload-local" into /workspace/test_emb.jpg and used --print to confirm.
- Verified retrieval with --verify; the embedded comment was correctly read back.

Files created/modified
- /workspace/embed_bug.py (new)
- /workspace/test.jpg and /workspace/test_emb.jpg were created during testing (you can remove them if not
needed).

Notes and next steps (optional enhancements)
- Consider embedding structured fields (e.g., JSON with explicit fields for reporter, OS, app version) by
default when --auto is used — already supported by the --auto flag.
- If you expect very large payloads, consider storing a checksum in EXIF and uploading the full payload 
to a central store, referencing it from EXIF.
- Optionally add simple signing/encryption of the embedded payload for integrity/confidentiality.

If you want, I can now:
- Add an option to compress or sign the payload before embedding.
- Add unit tests around embed/read functions.

